","sq"],["at","\nWest leads the @SQ against your contract of Four Hearts."],["pg",""],["lc","sq"],["pc","sq"],["hs","ss"],["nt","\nYou can afford three losers. You have two Spade losers, "],["pg",""],["ls","ss"],["hs","sh"],["at","a potential Heart loser, "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["hs","sc"],["at","and a Club loser. "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["hc","ca"],["at","If West has the @CA, "],["pg",""],["lc","ca"],["hs","nc"],["at","you can establish an extra winner in dummy on which to discard a loser. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["hc","sa"],["nt","\nHowever, that plan won't work because the opponents have already led a Spade. Once you take your @SA, "],["pg",""],["lc","sa"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sa"],["pg",""],["hs","ws"],["hs","es"],["at","the opponents will be able to take two Spade tricks "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","es"],["hc","ca"],["at","when they get in with the @CA before you have the opportunity to discard one."],["pg",""],["lc","ca"],["hs","sh"],["hs","nh"],["nt","\nInstead, you must plan to avoid losing a Heart trick. With nine cards in the combined hands, the maxim eight ever, nine never indicates that you should not take the finesse. "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["ls","nh"],["hc","hk"],["at","Play to the @HK "],["pg",""],["lc","hk"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","hk"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hc","ha"],["at","and then to the @HA, "],["pg",""],["lc","ha"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","ha"],["hc","hq"],["at","hoping to drop the @HQ."],["pg",""],["lc","hq"],["pc","hq"],["",""]]}}